Dane Backbier - dbackbie - dbackbie@u.rochester.edu - Lab 7 - Heaps

Lab 7 is aimed at implementing a heap ADT in Java. To test minHeap.java simply
compile and run the code(keeping assertions enabled). This is the expected output
(where all tests are passed):
1 3 8 5 4

4 5 8

insert and deleteMin methods passed

size and isEmpty methods passed

2 4 6 7 8

expand method passed

1 4 3 6 8 7

heapify method passed

All methods passed.

The parts of the output that are numbers are the outputs from the printHeap method.
The other files are the UR_Heap.java, which was implemented in minHeap.java. There
are also the class files from compiling the code, this README, and the lab instructions
pdf. There is no specific testing file as the unit tests are done in the main method
of minHeap.java.